                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3df6a5fe-4247-34ea-aab5-74353b430f69",
                        "entry_id": "1e575ed3-d3e7-326d-8c3d-5dad890df31f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "филос. направление в западноевропейской философии и литературе середины XX века, исследующее личный опыт, неповторимость человеческого существования, невыразимого на языке понятий, но интуитивно учитываемого каждым человеком при принятии важных решений"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad46c248-d395-415a-a5e9-ca847d1c570e",
                                "sense_id": "3df6a5fe-4247-34ea-aab5-74353b430f69",
                                "text": "― Помилуй, отец родной! ― пугаюсь я. ― А фиксы-то зачем? ― Экзистенциализм кипит в нашем герое, ― совсем не смущается Григорий."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "87e4a131-7696-46e4-b4f3-338a5ce1d312",
                        "source_entry_id": "1e575ed3-d3e7-326d-8c3d-5dad890df31f",
                        "source_sense_id": "3df6a5fe-4247-34ea-aab5-74353b430f69",
                        "target_lang_word": "existentialism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "existentialism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31c9c212-46e9-3af5-b4b0-49f181db20e1",
                                        "entry_id": "165049ff-f0e6-3def-ab5d-a83617a25763",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A twentieth-century philosophical movement emphasizing the uniqueness of each human existence in freely making its self-defining choices."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2eb5867a-a616-4d46-a609-8dd9a8d4b5a1",
                                                "sense_id": "31c9c212-46e9-3af5-b4b0-49f181db20e1",
                                                "text": "The heyday of existentialism occurred in the mid-twentieth century."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03b8c134-52cc-30ab-a923-cebcf5902dfb",
                                        "entry_id": "165049ff-f0e6-3def-ab5d-a83617a25763",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The philosophical views of a particular thinker associated with the existentialist movement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e094052c-cb7e-4325-8ed9-6d63dfff5a63",
                                                "sense_id": "03b8c134-52cc-30ab-a923-cebcf5902dfb",
                                                "text": "Sartre's existentialism is atheistic, but the existentialism of Marcel is distinctly Christian."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b4fb4b9-b7b9-4128-bbf4-048efc05f1a0",
                                                "sense_id": "03b8c134-52cc-30ab-a923-cebcf5902dfb",
                                                "text": "Instead of Existentialism, we should speak of Existentialisms."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "04a6d218-76a9-4e34-b653-a23fea8ecdf8",
                        "source_entry_id": "1e575ed3-d3e7-326d-8c3d-5dad890df31f",
                        "source_sense_id": "3df6a5fe-4247-34ea-aab5-74353b430f69",
                        "target_lang_word": "existencialismo",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "existencialismo",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cdb80f27-151d-3e47-9542-d27175609fba",
                                        "entry_id": "6a998255-25f8-355f-9f4a-fd591abda084",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Corriente de pensamiento que busca basar el conocimiento y lo real en la experiencia inmediata y única de existir y tomar decisiones, no en esencias o en metafísica. Se convierte en movimiento filosófico durante la primera mitad del siglo XX."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "127aa32e-1392-4ff8-97cc-d44b8cbced38",
                        "source_entry_id": "1e575ed3-d3e7-326d-8c3d-5dad890df31f",
                        "source_sense_id": "3df6a5fe-4247-34ea-aab5-74353b430f69",
                        "target_lang_word": "esistenzialismo",
                        "target_lang_code": "it",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "esistenzialismo",
                                "target_lang_code": "it",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2982227-05c0-3d21-a773-e340510ed490",
                                        "entry_id": "6c4cdc63-c544-3867-9292-7e904d6fbddb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "corrente di pensiero che si sofferma in gran parte sull'esistenza, sulla vita e su tutti i significati ad esse collegati; nata in Germania intorno al 1920 e diffusasi in Francia dopo la seconda guerra mondiale:"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd6cf83c-574b-45f3-9125-5e5a8e546e93",
                                                "sense_id": "a2982227-05c0-3d21-a773-e340510ed490",
                                                "text": "un filosofo che segue la corrente dell'esistenzialismo"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "736a8553-043b-4f8c-846d-1bd044663473",
                                                "sense_id": "a2982227-05c0-3d21-a773-e340510ed490",
                                                "text": "Introduzione agli esistenzialismi"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f7af1d3e-5e9c-453e-b78e-4891a61bf8ca",
                        "source_entry_id": "1e575ed3-d3e7-326d-8c3d-5dad890df31f",
                        "source_sense_id": "3df6a5fe-4247-34ea-aab5-74353b430f69",
                        "target_lang_word": "Existentialismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Existentialismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7161b6b2-c29c-38f3-87cf-ae5423816a33",
                                        "entry_id": "6616e85a-0555-3cc8-b92e-6046021d3491",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "eine in Frankreich entstandene philosophische Richtung des 20. Jahrhunderts, nach der im Gegensatz zum Essentialismus die Existenz Vorrang vor der Essenz hat"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30b1ea15-bd43-4c9e-a961-1f7c8b0b244c",
                                                "sense_id": "7161b6b2-c29c-38f3-87cf-ae5423816a33",
                                                "text": "In Begriffen wie Geworfenheit, Selbstentwurf, Freiheit und Selbstbestimmung zeigt sich die Zentrierung des Existentialismus auf das Problem der Befreiung des Menschen zu seinen eigenen Möglichkeiten hin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d8aa158-eee5-405b-8336-bc89821cbdeb",
                                                "sense_id": "7161b6b2-c29c-38f3-87cf-ae5423816a33",
                                                "text": "„Der junge Philosoph erklärte ihnen vor allem, was Existentialismus bedeutet.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2c955363-762c-4b2d-b51b-1486b61ef0a2",
                        "source_entry_id": "1e575ed3-d3e7-326d-8c3d-5dad890df31f",
